<section id="product" class="problem section shell" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / THE EVERYDAY BLIND SPOTS</div><h2 id="problem-title">Small details.<br> <span class="serif">Easy to miss.</span></h2></div><p>More products. More campaigns. More places for things to slip. Give your team a clear starting point for what needs a closer look.</p></div>
  <div class="issue-examples" aria-label="Fictional examples of catalog issues">
    <article><span class="issue-icon" aria-hidden="true">↔</span><h3>Will it fit?</h3><p>Sizes are listed, but the measurements are missing.</p></article>
    <article><span class="issue-icon" aria-hidden="true">≠</span><h3>Which detail is right?</h3><p>The title says two-piece. The description says three.</p></article>
    <article><span class="issue-icon" aria-hidden="true">%</span><h3>Does the offer add up?</h3><p>The banner says 30% off. The selling price doesn't.</p></article>
    <article><span class="issue-icon" aria-hidden="true">◷</span><h3>Is it ready to promote?</h3><p>The featured product is out of stock in most sizes.</p></article>
  </div>
  <p class="example-note">Demonstration examples. No real store has been audited.</p>
</section>

<section id="how-it-works" class="audit-section" data-controller="audit" aria-labelledby="audit-title">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / FROM FINDING TO NEXT STEP</div><h2 id="audit-title">Don't just spot it.<br> <span class="serif">Understand it.</span></h2></div><p>A useful recommendation starts with evidence. Follow one fictional product from a missing detail to a decision your team can make.</p></div>
    <div class="audit-layout">
      <div class="audit-steps">
        <article class="audit-step is-current" data-audit-target="step" id="audit-step-1"><span class="step-number">01</span><div><span class="eyebrow">THE PRODUCT</span><h3>A size label isn't<br> a size guide.</h3><p>Our example linen kurta has sizes S, M and L, but no garment measurements on the product page. A shopper is left to guess.</p><span class="step-tag">Catalog quality</span><div class="audit-inline-panel" data-audit-target="slot"></div></div></article>
        <article class="audit-step" data-audit-target="step" id="audit-step-2"><span class="step-number">02</span><div><span class="eyebrow">THE EVIDENCE</span><h3>See exactly<br> what needs a look.</h3><p>The example page lists three sizes. The description and size-guide link provide no chest or length measurements. That's the finding—not a claim about why shoppers leave.</p><span class="step-tag">Source: illustrative product page</span><div class="audit-inline-panel" data-audit-target="slot"></div></div></article>
        <article class="audit-step" data-audit-target="step" id="audit-step-3"><span class="step-number">03</span><div><span class="eyebrow">THE RECOMMENDATION</span><h3>A useful next step.<br> No invented facts.</h3><p>Ask the catalog team to verify the chest and length measurements for each size, then add the approved guide. Sellora won't invent garment details.</p><span class="step-tag">Measurements require verification</span><div class="audit-inline-panel" data-audit-target="slot"></div></div></article>
        <article class="audit-step" data-audit-target="step" id="audit-step-4"><span class="step-number">04</span><div><span class="eyebrow">THE TEAM'S REVIEW</span><h3>Your judgment.<br> Your final say.</h3><p>Review the evidence and exact proposed update with your team. Approved pilot actions keep a before-and-after record when they are applied to Shopify.</p><span class="step-tag">Reviewed action workflow</span><div class="audit-inline-panel" data-audit-target="slot"></div></div></article>
      </div>
      <div class="audit-sticky">
        <div class="audit-demo">
          <div class="demo-top"><span>Catalog review</span><span class="demo-label">ILLUSTRATIVE DEMO</span></div>
          <div class="audit-product"><%= image_tag "linen-kurta.webp", alt: "Ivory linen kurta used in the fictional catalog review", width: 960, height: 1280, loading: "lazy" %><div><span class="micro">STUDIO COLLECTION / 001</span><h3>Everyday<br> linen kurta</h3><p>Ivory · PKR 4,800</p><div class="sizes" aria-label="Example available sizes"><span>S</span><span>M</span><span>L</span></div><span class="missing-detail">↗ Size measurements missing</span></div></div>
          <div data-audit-target="panels">
          <div class="audit-panel" data-audit-target="panel"><span class="eyebrow">01 / FINDING</span><h4>Give shoppers a clearer picture.</h4><p>Sizes are available. The measurements aren't.</p><div class="evidence-line"><span>Size guide</span><strong>Not provided</strong></div></div>
          <div class="audit-panel" data-audit-target="panel" hidden><span class="eyebrow">02 / EVIDENCE</span><h4>Three sizes. No measurements.</h4><p>Example page: description + size-guide link</p><div class="evidence-line"><span>Chest / garment length</span><strong>Not found</strong></div></div>
          <div class="audit-panel" data-audit-target="panel" hidden><span class="eyebrow">03 / SUGGESTED ACTION</span><h4>Add a verified size guide.</h4><p>Ask your team for chest and length measurements for S, M and L.</p><div class="evidence-line"><span>Garment facts</span><strong>Team to verify</strong></div></div>
          <div class="audit-panel" data-audit-target="panel" hidden><span class="eyebrow">04 / REVIEW PREVIEW</span><h4>Ready for a human decision.</h4><p>Before: no guide. Proposed: team-verified measurements. Nothing is published.</p><div class="evidence-line"><span>Store changes</span><strong>None applied</strong></div></div>
          </div>
          <nav class="audit-progress" aria-label="Catalog demonstration steps"><a href="#audit-step-1" data-audit-target="marker" aria-current="step"><span>01</span> Product</a><a href="#audit-step-2" data-audit-target="marker"><span>02</span> Evidence</a><a href="#audit-step-3" data-audit-target="marker"><span>03</span> Suggestion</a><a href="#audit-step-4" data-audit-target="marker"><span>04</span> Review</a></nav>
        </div>
        <p class="example-note">A product concept, using fictional information and an AI-created garment image.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="signals section shell" aria-labelledby="signals-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / THE FULLER PICTURE</div><h2 id="signals-title">Attention isn't<br> <span class="serif">the whole story.</span></h2></div><p>Follow the journey from being seen to being bought. Planned sales monitoring will connect shopping activity, size availability and final order outcomes.</p></div>
  <div class="journey" data-controller="reveal">
    <div class="journey-heading"><strong>From first look to final outcome</strong><span class="demo-label">ILLUSTRATIVE DATA · 7 DAYS</span></div>
    <ol class="journey-stages">
      <li><span class="journey-category">ATTENTION</span><span class="journey-value">12,000</span><h3>Product exposures</h3><div class="journey-bar" style="--bar: 100%"></div><p>Times a product was shown in a tracked placement.</p></li>
      <li><span class="journey-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="journey-category">INTEREST</span><span class="journey-value">2,400</span><h3>Product views</h3><div class="journey-bar" style="--bar: 20%"></div><p>Recorded visits to a product's detail page.</p></li>
      <li><span class="journey-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="journey-category">PURCHASE INTENT</span><span class="journey-value">320</span><h3>Cart actions</h3><div class="journey-bar" style="--bar: 2.67%"></div><p>Recorded product additions to a shopping cart.</p></li>
      <li><span class="journey-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="journey-category">PURCHASE INTENT</span><span class="journey-value">180</span><h3>Checkouts started</h3><div class="journey-bar" style="--bar: 1.5%"></div><p>Checkout starts, before payment or fulfillment.</p></li>
      <li><span class="journey-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="journey-category">ORDER OUTCOME</span><span class="journey-value">96</span><h3>Final sales</h3><div class="journey-bar" style="--bar: 0.8%"></div><p>Illustrative delivered orders with payment collected and no refund recorded.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="journey-note"><span>Read the signals together.</span><p>More views don't explain fewer carts. A checkout isn't payment. A placed COD order isn't collected revenue.</p></div>
  </div>
  <details class="data-notes"><summary>What these example numbers do—and don't—tell you <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>These are fictional counts from one seven-day window, not a matched customer cohort or a conversion-rate report. The bars share a 12,000-exposure reference scale; they do not establish conversion rates. Event counts can include repeat activity. Final sales exclude orders still awaiting delivery or collection; later cancellations and refunds can change outcomes.</p><p>Actual coverage will depend on authorized integrations, consent, browser blockers and source availability. Low traffic alone doesn't establish low demand, and abandonment doesn't establish a cause. Revenue isn't profit; profit reporting would also require costs.</p></details>
</section>
